==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɒkɪt|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-socket.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒkɪt|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|xno|en}} ''[[soket]]'', "[[spearhead]]" (diminutive of {{etyl|fro|en}} ''[[soc]]'': [[plowshare]]), from {{etyl|VL.|en}} ''[[soccus]]''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|mechanics|lang=en}} An opening into which a [[plug]] or other connecting part is designed to fit (e.g. ''a [[light bulb]] socket'').
# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} A [[hollow]] into a [[bone]] which a part fits, such as an [[eye]], or another bone, in the case of a [[joint]].
# {{context|computing|lang=en}} A [[two-way]] [[named pipe]] on Unix and Unix-like systems, used for [[interprocess communication]].

